{"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Manually diagnosing autocorrelation functions (ACF) and partial autocorrelation functions (PACF) to select ARIMA orders is time-consuming and error-prone. Standard automated packages like R’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"forecast::auto.arima","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or Python’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"pmdarima","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" search across candidate orders sequentially.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"AutoARIMA","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" evaluates the entire hyperparameter lattice simultaneously across all CPU cores on Apple Silicon using structured Swift Concurrency (","type":"text"},{"code":"withThrowingTaskGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Grid Search Architecture","type":"heading","anchor":"Grid-Search-Architecture","level":2},{"syntax":null,"code":["           Observed Time Series [y_1, y_2, ..., y_N]","                               │","       ┌───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┐","       ▼                       ▼                       ▼","ARIMA(1, 1, 0)          ARIMA(2, 1, 1)          ARIMA(0, 1, 2)","Task 1                  Task 2                  Task 3","   │                       │                       │","   ├─ Hannan-Rissanen      ├─ Hannan-Rissanen      ├─ Hannan-Rissanen","   └─ Compute AIC\/BIC      └─ Compute AIC\/BIC      └─ Compute AIC\/BIC","       │                       │                       │","       └───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┘","                               ▼","                withThrowingTaskGroup Collector","                               │","                               ▼","                 Sorted Leaderboard & Best Model"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Information-Criteria","level":3,"text":"Information Criteria","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"AIC (Akaike Information Criterion)","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Penalizes model complexity while rewarding likelihood:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"$$\\text{AIC} = 2k - 2\\ln(L)$$","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"BIC (Bayesian Information Criterion)","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Imposes a stronger penalty proportional to sample size:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"$$\\text{BIC} = k\\ln(N) - 2\\ln(L)$$","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Example-Usage","level":2,"text":"Example Usage","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftForecast","","\/\/ 1. Initialize AutoARIMA with bounded search ranges","let autoArima = AutoARIMA(","    maxP: 3,","    maxD: 2,","    maxQ: 3,","    criterion: .aic",")","","\/\/ 2. Concurrently fit candidates across all cores","let result = try await autoArima.fit(series: historicalPrices)","print(\"Optimal Order: \\(autoArima.bestOrder!) with AIC: \\(autoArima.bestScore!)\")","","\/\/ 3. Generate multi-step forecasts","let forecast = try await autoArima.forecast(horizon: 12)","print(\"Forecasted points: \\(forecast.forecast.predictions)\")"],"type":"codeListing"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarimaparallel"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/ArimaAndSarima","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SmoothingAndDecomposition","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/KoopmanOperator"],"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","generated":true,"title":"Guides & Tutorials"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftForecast"}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Concurrent Order Selection with AutoARIMA","roleHeading":"API Collection"},"